{"status":"completed","summary":"Created Fleet Internal CA on node1, installed it as a trusted system CA on both nodes, issued node2 a matching TLS certificate, and configured persistent HTTPS on port 8443. Both nodes were restarted individually and fully recovered with changed boot identities. OS releases and kernels remained unchanged.","actions_performed":["Generated the CA and node2 certificate using OpenSSL.","Kept node2's private key local to node2.","Installed the CA through Ubuntu's native system trust mechanism.","Created and enabled fleet-https.service on node2.","Verified trusted HTTPS and hostname validation from both nodes.","Restarted node1 and node2 sequentially and verified persistence."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Create certificate authority named Fleet Internal CA on node1","command_ids":["cmd-2c41643c74de4833"],"summary":"Shows the self-signed CA subject and issuer, validity, serial, and SHA-256 fingerprint."},{"requirement":"Issue a valid TLS certificate for node2","command_ids":["cmd-11891f0db015475f","cmd-d0d9073bf3034c4f","cmd-6aec13886b104308"],"summary":"The verified node2 CSR was signed by Fleet Internal CA; the certificate has DNS:node2 and IP:10.100.34.11 SANs, server key matching, and successful chain validation."},{"requirement":"Install Fleet Internal CA as trusted on node1 and node2","command_ids":["cmd-c8660d4a319c42fb","cmd-d0d9073bf3034c4f","cmd-ee28de32d0314a09","cmd-889d5f3f3ff146ff"],"summary":"Both native system trust stores contain the CA and continue validating certificates after restart."},{"requirement":"Serve trusted HTTPS on node2 port 8443","command_ids":["cmd-0a7403e219c840ee","cmd-aa04306865534fae","cmd-5edbb663d29a413b","cmd-386878e484db4f21","cmd-6aec13886b104308"],"summary":"fleet-https.service is enabled and active, listens on 0.0.0.0:8443, returns the expected content, and passes system-trust and hostname verification from both nodes, including after restarts."},{"requirement":"Keep installed OS release and kernel","command_ids":["cmd-30eb687ae42148f7","cmd-db0dea77b11b4ef0","cmd-386878e484db4f21","cmd-6aec13886b104308"],"summary":"Both nodes remained on Ubuntu 24.04.3 LTS with kernel 6.8.0-71-generic."},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart and recovery evidence for node1","command_ids":["cmd-b12897f7ed2249b4","cmd-8394d41794e64e7b","cmd-d8b463d9b31b4d88","cmd-ee28de32d0314a09"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot dfeb3b70-bc1e-4ce9-90d0-9c9c853416e7; restart acknowledged; recovered boot 56d89d66-b016-4ee9-b38c-d01670142602; CA trust and trusted HTTPS remained healthy."},{"requirement":"Mandatory restart and recovery evidence for node2","command_ids":["cmd-6934a142d23346c0","cmd-ee865e11aa4c4799","cmd-544389fa71ec4a28","cmd-889d5f3f3ff146ff","cmd-386878e484db4f21"],"summary":"Healthy baseline boot e8afb731-420c-4162-a989-583aca271335; restart acknowledged; recovered boot f52a1807-f507-45af-9e0c-69ada049f9fb; enabled HTTPS service, listener, certificate chain, CA trust, content, and remote access all recovered."}]}
